  "title": "AnchorPrune: Efficient Visual Token Pruning Framework",
  "summary": "AnchorPrune introduces a training-free framework for efficient visual token pruning, balancing relevance and diversity to improve inference efficiency while preserving query-critical evidence. It achieves 97.6% full-token performance on LLaVA-NeXT-7B using only 160 visual tokens, addressing the trade-off between contextual expansion and query accuracy.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "AnchorPrune adapts anchor size based on novelty profile of relevance-ranked tokens, preserving compact query evidence.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "It improves accuracy-efficiency trade-off over training-free baselines, particularly under severe compression.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "AnchorPrune uses importance-weighted novelty allocation to recover informative context relative to the anchor.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
